# ─── Meridian PMS — Environment Variables ─────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# After setting up .env, run:
#   npx prisma generate          # Generate Prisma client
#   npx prisma db push           # Push schema to database (use DIRECT_URL)
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Database (Supabase PostgreSQL) ─────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. Use the TRANSACTION pooler connection string from Supabase.
#
# Where to find it:
#   Supabase Dashboard → Settings → Database → Connection string → URI tab
#   → Select "Transaction mode" (port 6543 on the pooler host)
#
# IMPORTANT: Do NOT use Session mode (port 5432) — it has a hard limit of
# 15 concurrent connections and causes EMAXCONNSESSION errors under load.
# Transaction mode releases connections after each transaction, allowing
# hundreds of concurrent requests on the same 15-connection pool.
#
# SSL is AUTOMATICALLY enforced (sslmode=verify-full with embedded CA cert).
# The CA certificate is embedded in src/lib/db.ts — works on Vercel, Render,
# Docker, Railway, Fly.io, and any Node.js platform. No external cert files needed.
#
# Example (Transaction mode, port 6543):
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abc123:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true
#
# Example (Session mode, port 5432 — AVOID unless you know what you're doing):
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abc123:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?pgbouncer=true
#
DATABASE_URL=

# ─── Direct Database URL (for Prisma migrations only) ───────
# OPTIONAL. Required ONLY if you need to run prisma db push / prisma migrate deploy
# from environments where the pooler URL doesn't support DDL.
#
# Where to find it:
#   Supabase Dashboard → Settings → Database → Connection string → URI tab
#   → Select "Direct connection" (port 5432, non-pooler host db.abc123.supabase.co)
#
# Usage:
#   DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:[PASSWORD]@db.abc123.supabase.co:5432/postgres
#   npx prisma db push  # Uses DIRECT_DATABASE_URL if set, falls back to DATABASE_URL
#
# NOTE: Render's build command auto-switches pooler port 5432 → 6543 for migrations.
#       Vercel: Run prisma db push locally before deploying.
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=

# ─── JWT Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. Strong random string (64+ chars). Used to sign HS256 access tokens.
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# JWT_SECRET=

# ─── Optional: Redis (for distributed rate limiting) ────────
# Without Redis: rate limiting & auth cache are per-instance only (works fine for single instance)
# With Redis: distributed rate limiting, shared auth cache across multiple instances
# Recommended for 2+ instances or 1000+ concurrent users.
# Use rediss:// (TLS) in production.
# REDIS_URL=rediss://default:[PASSWORD]@redis-host:6379

# ─── Optional: Supabase Realtime ────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for live room status, reservation, payment updates.
#
# OPTION A (recommended — zero-hop): Set NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars so the client
# can initialize WebSocket immediately without an API round-trip.
# This saves ~100-200ms on every realtime initialization.
# In Vercel: Settings → Environment Variables → add both.
# In Render: Environment → add both.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://abc123.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
#
# OPTION B (fallback — one HTTP hop): Set server-side vars only.
# The client will call GET /api/config/realtime to discover the URL.
# This adds ~100-200ms but keeps the anon key out of the HTML source.
#
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
